The first long run stopped at the first feasible Q27 packet; the tail and
repair runs complete the exact four-deletion census.

A. Q27-only four-deletion census

Model:
  CORE = 7*{1,...,12}
  delete_count = 4
  add_budget = 5
  candidate_window = 1..1092
  primitive constraint = at least one added speed not divisible by 7
  Q27 = {d*m: d in {1,2,7,14}, 1 <= m <= 27} \ {1}

Exact deletion-set result:
  total deletion sets = binom(12,4) = 495
  Q27-infeasible deletion sets = 493
  Q27-feasible deletion sets = 2
  unresolved after sparse repair = 0

The 12 short-cap unknowns from the first/tail runs were all repaired to
infeasible with a 120s cap:

  (14,21,28,70), (14,21,28,84), (14,21,70,84),
  (14,28,42,70), (14,28,56,70), (14,28,56,84),
  (14,56,70,84), (21,28,56,70), (21,28,56,84),
  (21,28,70,84), (21,56,70,84), (28,42,70,84).

